cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its published evidence, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Evidence guarded speech measurement"
abstract: >-
  An open research project on speech measurement that records where every input
  came from, carries uncertainty beside every number, and refuses to produce a
  result when the evidence, the reference or the validation is inadequate. It
  includes a reproducible audit of how pronunciation measurement behaves across
  declared English reference varieties, and an implementation of the provenance,
  abstention and claim verification machinery that audit needs. It makes no
  screening or clinical claim.
authors:
